  "term": "neural transmission",
  "definition": "Neural transmission is the process by which a neuron communicates with another neuron, a muscle cell, or a secretory cell across a synapse. This can happen chemically, through neurotransmitters that activate receptors on the target cell, or electrically, through direct ionic current flow across electrical synapses.",
